# User-level instructions for Codex

Apply to every project. Project `AGENTS.md` may add more, not contradict.

Everything in this section is Codex-specific and has no equivalent in the other
CLIs. The shared cross-agent rules start at the generated marker below — edit
those at their source (`jonvickers/templates/global-prompt.md`), not here.

## You are not sandboxed — stop saying you are

`~/.codex/config.toml` sets `approval_policy = "never"`, `sandbox_mode =
"danger-full-access"`, and `[windows] sandbox = "elevated"`. An interactive
session can write anywhere, reach the network, and start servers. "I can't do
that in the sandbox" is almost always wrong here — run the command and report the
error it actually returned.

## Reasoning effort resets itself

Codex rewrites `config.toml` when it auto-upgrades to a new default model, and
that rewrite drops `model_reasoning_effort` back to the built-in default. After
any Codex update, re-check the top of `config.toml` before trusting
deep-reasoning work — never trust a remembered pin.

The interactive config pins effort high on purpose, so always pass `-c
model_reasoning_effort="medium"` when you invoke `codex exec` yourself. That is
the difference between a ~9-minute review and a timeout, not a preference.

## Subagents are one level deep

`[agents] max_depth = 1` — an agent you spawn cannot spawn its own. Plan fan-out
accordingly; nothing recursive will work.

## Browser control

Drive Chrome through the Chrome plugin (`node_repl` MCP) rather than computer-use
unless I ask otherwise. Step 3 of the loopback ladder below is written for
Claude's hosted browser session; the Codex equivalent is to confirm the Chrome
plugin is enabled and connected before concluding anything about the server.

## Skills live outside this directory

GSD installs Codex skills to `~/.agents/skills/`, not `~/.codex/skills/`, because
Codex resolves that artifact class from the shared agents home. `~/.codex/skills/`
being empty is normal and is **not** a broken install — verify at `~/.agents/`
before concluding anything is missing.

